    {
      "@id": "https://knoedg.nyc/inside-the-map-of-30-immigrant-enclaves/#claim-moia-series",
      "@type": "schema:Claim",
      "schema:text": "The Mayor’s Office of Immigrant Affairs published an Immigrant Enclave Illustration Series from 2023-04-17, and states in its own end-of-tenure report that 23 illustrations were published. “Little Italy” does not appear anywhere in that 85-page report.",
      "schema:citation": {
        "@id": "https://www.nyc.gov/assets/immigrants/downloads/pdf/digital-spread-12-31-2025-moia-impact.pdf"
      },
      "schema:additionalProperty": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "KEE lifecycle state",
          "schema:value": "Active"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "KEE confidence",
          "schema:value": 0.93
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "Illustrations stated",
          "schema:value": 23
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://knoedg.nyc/inside-the-map-of-30-immigrant-enclaves/#claim-delta",
      "@type": "schema:Claim",
      "schema:text": "Comparing the two, exactly five names appear on the map and nowhere in that report: Little Egypt, Little Odessa, Little Palestine, Little Poland, Little Senegal. The remaining difference is structural. The map is an extension of the series, not a subset of it. Who made the additions is not established.",
      "schema:citation": {
        "@id": "https://www.nyc.gov/assets/immigrants/downloads/pdf/digital-spread-12-31-2025-moia-impact.pdf"
      },
      "schema:additionalProperty": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "KEE lifecycle state",
          "schema:value": "Active"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "KEE confidence",
          "schema:value": 0.9
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "Names added",
          "schema:value": 5
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "Derivation",
          "schema:value": "Derived by comparison of two retrieved primary documents, not retrieved as a claim from either."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://knoedg.nyc/inside-the-map-of-30-immigrant-enclaves/#claim-criterion-demographic",
      "@type": "schema:Claim",
      "schema:text": "A city spokesperson, quoted by one outlet, said the map “highlights neighborhoods in New York City that have substantial foreign-born populations from regions and countries around the world.” This criterion asks how many residents of a neighborhood today were born abroad. It appears in no published rule.",
      "schema:citation": {
        "@id": "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/policy/immigration/4641977/mamdani-map-nyc-immigrant-outrage-italian-community/"
      },
      "schema:additionalProperty": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "KEE lifecycle state",
          "schema:value": "Active"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "KEE confidence",
          "schema:value": 0.7
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "Relationship to the heritage criterion",
          "schema:value": "Definition mismatch — examined and found to be a difference in what each criterion asks, not a disagreement."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://knoedg.nyc/inside-the-map-of-30-immigrant-enclaves/#claim-criterion-heritage",
      "@type": "schema:Claim",
      "schema:text": "Critics, quoted by the press, treat a neighborhood’s history of immigrant settlement as the basis for inclusion, regardless of how many residents were born abroad today. This criterion also appears in no published rule.",
      "schema:citation": {
        "@id": "https://www.theblaze.com/news/wheres-little-italy-mamdanis-immigrant-enclave-map-sparks-backlash"
      },
      "schema:additionalProperty": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "KEE lifecycle state",
          "schema:value": "Active"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "KEE confidence",
          "schema:value": 0.65
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "Relationship to the demographic criterion",
          "schema:value": "Definition mismatch — the two ask different questions of the same neighborhoods."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://knoedg.nyc/inside-the-map-of-30-immigrant-enclaves/#claim-dcp-threshold",
      "@type": "schema:Claim",
      "schema:text": "A published threshold does exist elsewhere. The Department of City Planning’s 2026 report defines a “major immigrant neighborhood” as one whose foreign-born density exceeds the city average, using a threshold of 40 percent, and records SoHo-Little Italy at 30.5 percent. The report scopes that definition to its own chapter, and nothing found connects it to this map.",
      "schema:citation": {
        "@id": "https://www.nyc.gov/assets/planning/newest-new-yorkers-2026/Ch3.html"
      },
      "schema:additionalProperty": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "KEE lifecycle state",
          "schema:value": "Active"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "KEE confidence",
          "schema:value": 0.94
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "Threshold",
          "schema:value": "40 percent foreign-born"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "SoHo-Little Italy foreign-born share",
          "schema:value": 30.5
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "Applies to this map",
          "schema:value": "Not established. The report scopes the definition to its own chapter."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://knoedg.nyc/inside-the-map-of-30-immigrant-enclaves/#claim-amendment",
      "@type": "schema:Claim",
      "schema:text": "On 2026-07-10 the mayor said the map was “initially created by the prior administration in 2023” and that “we’re going to be making additional changes in the future … and that includes adding Little Italy to the map.” That is a commitment to a future change. No amended version has been located. The map file itself is byte-identical to an archived copy taken before the criticism, so this artifact was not amended.",
      "schema:citation": {
        "@id": "https://www.amny.com/news/little-italy-mamdani-immigrant-map-backlash/"
      },
      "schema:additionalProperty": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "KEE lifecycle state",
          "schema:value": "Active"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "KEE confidence",
          "schema:value": 0.72
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "schema:name": "Amendment observed",
          "schema:value": "No. The artifact is byte-identical across a window containing the whole controversy. This does not establish that no amended version exists at another address."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://knoedg.nyc/inside-the-map-of-30-immigrant-enclaves/#claim-host-page",
      "@type": "schema:Claim",
      "schema:text": "Checked on 2026-08-20, the URL that carried the map redirects to the program index, and that index mentions neither the program nor the map, while the map file itself is still served. Why the URL now redirects is not established. Archived copies of the page from mid-June and from 2026-07-08 still carry the map, so it was on the page on the day the criticism was first reported.",
      "schema:citation": {
        "@id": "https://www.nyctourism.com/worldcup26/the-nyc-neighborhood-passport-world-cup-program/"
      },
      "schema:additionalProperty": [
